 "best_idea": "Let armour soak a fixed share of each hit (a third or a half) from a points pool that clears when it runs out, and compute any push from the raw damage before the immunity gate, so the push is decided even when damage is not.",
 "decision": "adapt",
 "decision_why": "Armour as a points pool that soaks a fixed share and clears when used up is a small testable rule that fits one ledger in the damage step; push is adapted as a server stagger state, never a position push; the aim window is not decided here.",
 "decision_status": "proposed",
 "acceptance": "A server test sets 9 class-1 armour points and a 30 hit: 9 is absorbed, 21 reaches health, the armour class is cleared; a 1000-point hit is not absorbed by invulnerability."
